1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,000
It all started with a single statement from Elma.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
I demand improved working conditions!

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,000
What's this about? Are you hangry?

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,000
This company wants too much overtime, and you know it!

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,000
The workload required of each individual is absolutely...

6
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,000
It's not that Elma's demands were unjustified.

7
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,000
We just didn't have a say in our scheduling.

8
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Plus, our company's already made some solid improvements since its founding.

9
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
It took some time, but the working conditions have improved.

10
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000
And compared to how things used to be, the amount of work seems like a fair exchange.

11
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,000
I tried to explain this to her, but...

12
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,000
You can't just give up and accept this abuse!

13
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:39,000
I refuse to give in!

14
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:42,000
I'm gonna fight for our freedom!

15
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Surrounded by those of us who had grown accustomed to exploitative labor

16
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,000
and living out our days aimlessly, Elma took a stand all by herself.

17
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Good luck!

18
00:02:21,957 --> 00:02:31,057
Two days later, Elma used the few moments she had in between assignments to create a proposal for improved working conditions.

19
00:02:31,837 --> 00:02:35,317
I was once again astonished by how capable dragons could be.

20
00:02:37,797 --> 00:02:38,317
However...

21
00:02:38,317 --> 00:02:40,237
You're laughing at me!

22
00:02:41,537 --> 00:02:43,297
You want to expand personnel?

23
00:02:43,657 --> 00:02:44,037
Yes!

24
00:02:44,297 --> 00:02:47,977
We're currently doing mid-career recruitment and there's not a single applicant.

25
00:02:48,197 --> 00:02:48,797
Why's that?

26
00:02:48,797 --> 00:02:52,037
Because of the programming language we're expected to use at this company.

27
00:02:53,177 --> 00:02:56,257
Even if we hired new grads, they'd still need a training period.

28
00:02:56,397 --> 00:02:57,737
But they'd catch up quickly, right?

29
00:02:57,997 --> 00:02:59,517
Not everyone is like you.

30
00:03:00,257 --> 00:03:00,837
Here you go.

31
00:03:01,397 --> 00:03:03,117
Try again taking all that into account.

32
00:03:05,637 --> 00:03:07,077
I finished the revisions!

33
00:03:07,217 --> 00:03:08,017
That was fast!

34
00:03:09,057 --> 00:03:13,277
I was surprised by her speed, but it was the content that really left me shocked.

35
00:03:13,277 --> 00:03:15,617
The rough spots had been completely revised.

36
00:03:15,617 --> 00:03:19,777
None of the sections had any contradictions, and the text was organized perfectly.

37
00:03:20,617 --> 00:03:21,757
This is great!

38
00:03:21,877 --> 00:03:22,597
You mean that?

39
00:03:22,937 --> 00:03:24,757
Submit it to our department head right away.

40
00:03:24,897 --> 00:03:25,657
I'm on it!

41
00:03:28,397 --> 00:03:29,477
It's a no-go.

42
00:03:30,497 --> 00:03:33,637
He gave her some babble about the company's income and expenditures.

43
00:03:33,997 --> 00:03:35,817
Things programmers don't even deal with.

44
00:03:35,957 --> 00:03:37,097
And she couldn't fight back.

45
00:03:37,857 --> 00:03:41,277
I could tell she was getting emotional about it, so I hit her with one of these.

46
00:03:42,857 --> 00:03:43,857
Damn it!

47
00:03:43,857 --> 00:03:48,017
I revised it again!

48
00:03:48,577 --> 00:03:49,797
There's something wrong with you!

49
00:03:50,697 --> 00:03:55,417
We were all overwhelmed by Elma's intensity as we began reading through the latest draft.

50
00:03:56,557 --> 00:03:57,517
It was epic.

51
00:03:58,057 --> 00:04:03,157
She had listed every individual's schedule in detail, including bathroom breaks, midday fatigue,

52
00:04:03,357 --> 00:04:07,397
time away from workspaces, and even the amount of time resting their heads on their elbows

53
00:04:07,397 --> 00:04:09,017
or recrossing their legs.

54
00:04:09,017 --> 00:04:13,237
It was laid out like a curse disguised as a proposal to improve efficiency.

55
00:04:13,777 --> 00:04:18,677
It was a testament to our complete lack of privacy that many employees felt it would have been more humane

56
00:04:18,677 --> 00:04:22,957
for our boss to publish nude photos of them on the company website without their permission.

57
00:04:24,097 --> 00:04:25,497
How did she get all this information?

58
00:04:26,377 --> 00:04:27,737
According to her...

59
00:04:27,737 --> 00:04:29,097
I used my clairvoyance.

60
00:04:29,577 --> 00:04:31,897
I made my vision a thousand-screen multi-display.

61
00:04:31,897 --> 00:04:36,057
Even her analogies were being influenced by work.

62
00:04:36,857 --> 00:04:39,397
She triumphantly headed to submit her proposal again.

63
00:04:39,857 --> 00:04:44,657
Shocking content aside, it was thorough and convincing enough to serve in negotiations.

64
00:04:45,757 --> 00:04:48,417
Maybe half-day Fridays could be more than just a dream.

65
00:04:48,417 --> 00:04:55,897
Still, it could be trauma bonding, but I don't know how I'll be able to relax if I don't work at least eight hours.

66
00:04:56,477 --> 00:04:57,617
That's sad.

67
00:04:59,037 --> 00:05:01,977
However, the dream was only alive for a short time.

68
00:05:03,017 --> 00:05:06,777
All three of us were surprised when we were summoned by the executive director.

69
00:05:07,637 --> 00:05:09,217
He wasn't going to fire us, was he?

70
00:05:10,297 --> 00:05:14,457
We headed to his office with anxiety on our faces and terror in our hearts.

71
00:05:17,157 --> 00:05:17,877
Come in.

72
00:05:18,417 --> 00:05:19,517
It's us!

73
00:05:22,097 --> 00:05:22,657
Hey.

74
00:05:23,397 --> 00:05:25,617
I hear you've been very kind to Shota.

75
00:05:26,417 --> 00:05:27,297
Oh, no.

76
00:05:28,397 --> 00:05:30,017
That's Shota Baby's father.

77
00:05:30,497 --> 00:05:31,637
Isn't he a mage or something?

78
00:05:32,957 --> 00:05:35,057
Did you have a look at the improvement proposal?

79
00:05:35,797 --> 00:05:36,317
Yes.

80
00:05:36,537 --> 00:05:38,317
You did a very good job on it overall.

81
00:05:38,677 --> 00:05:39,737
Joey Elma, right?

82
00:05:40,377 --> 00:05:41,117
Forgive me.

83
00:05:42,337 --> 00:05:44,537
Would you prefer Priestess of the Holy Seas?

84
00:05:44,537 --> 00:05:44,897
Huh?

85
00:05:44,897 --> 00:05:49,977
I'm currently an employee here, so whichever you prefer.

86
00:05:50,977 --> 00:05:53,177
Would you mind telling us what this is all about?

87
00:05:53,697 --> 00:05:55,797
Honestly, it's about the goddess Shota summoned.

88
00:05:56,477 --> 00:06:00,637
See, I figured if you were her friends, then I should be familiar with you, too.

89
00:06:00,637 --> 00:06:03,177
I bet she's ruining your son's education, isn't she?

90
00:06:03,177 --> 00:06:04,577
What a perv.

91
00:06:04,577 --> 00:06:06,297
She's also an ex-goddess.

92
00:06:06,297 --> 00:06:10,617
We have a rule in our family that we take responsibility for our summons.

93
00:06:10,617 --> 00:06:16,677
And contrary to your belief, I think the lady is good for Shota's education in many ways.

94
00:06:16,857 --> 00:06:20,337
Be sure to thank her when he develops a fetish for older, questionable women.

95
00:06:22,037 --> 00:06:24,137
All right, my friends.

96
00:06:24,437 --> 00:06:27,577
I think now would be a good time to discuss business, yes?

97
00:06:27,577 --> 00:06:30,697
That sucks.

98
00:06:31,157 --> 00:06:32,477
I was hoping he'd go for it.

99
00:06:33,137 --> 00:06:34,637
People would complain if he did.

100
00:06:34,917 --> 00:06:37,137
It wouldn't be fair for only our department to improve.

101
00:06:37,597 --> 00:06:38,957
He at least got that portion right.

102
00:06:39,677 --> 00:06:41,937
Hey, I'm just glad he took the time to look it over.

103
00:06:42,657 --> 00:06:47,337
I've noticed we've been getting out on time more frequently, so obviously he's taking some of it.

104
00:06:47,337 --> 00:06:47,877
That doesn't matter!

105
00:06:48,077 --> 00:06:48,717
It's not enough!

106
00:06:48,937 --> 00:06:52,077
This company is an ethical nightmare, and it's up to us to turn it around!

107
00:06:52,437 --> 00:06:53,577
Did that come out of you?

108
00:06:54,057 --> 00:06:56,197
As you clutch your bag of hush money chocolates?

109
00:06:56,197 --> 00:06:58,977
That is that, and this is this! Chocolates are low in sugar!

110
00:06:59,297 --> 00:07:00,637
That doesn't make any sense.

111
00:07:02,777 --> 00:07:06,357
Even after accepting his bribe, Elma refused to give up.

112
00:07:07,437 --> 00:07:09,597
She tried to start a labor union on site.

113
00:07:10,217 --> 00:07:15,477
She created a safe space for employee discussion and continued to advocate for better working conditions.

114
00:07:16,697 --> 00:07:20,477
What surprised me most was that Toru was helping her with that.

115
00:07:21,177 --> 00:07:24,977
I think it's a great plan, and if it works out, you'll be able to come home to me earlier!

116
00:07:24,977 --> 00:07:26,857
It all makes sense now.

117
00:07:26,897 --> 00:07:28,837
And if it doesn't work out, she'll...

118
00:07:28,837 --> 00:07:30,697
Back at you!

119
00:07:31,557 --> 00:07:36,497
Seeing rival forces cooperating for mutual benefit gave me hope that maybe it could work.

120
00:07:36,957 --> 00:07:39,857
However, our executive director was crafty.

121
00:07:40,017 --> 00:07:44,477
He used both logic and delusions in perfect ratios to sidestep every claim.

122
00:07:44,477 --> 00:07:49,037
Damn it!

123
00:07:49,337 --> 00:07:51,457
This is so unfair!

124
00:07:52,637 --> 00:07:53,737
Elma, are you...

125
00:07:53,737 --> 00:07:54,877
No, I'm not okay!

126
00:07:55,117 --> 00:07:57,757
I shouldn't have to work so late and always miss the limited sweets!

127
00:07:58,317 --> 00:07:59,537
That's what this is about?

128
00:07:59,537 --> 00:08:09,337
I've finally finished work in enough time to experience those limited-time flavors!

129
00:08:09,577 --> 00:08:10,357
It's a miracle!

130
00:08:11,377 --> 00:08:12,497
Three of those, please!

131
00:08:12,617 --> 00:08:13,197
Three of them!

132
00:08:13,737 --> 00:08:14,437
Two, please!

133
00:08:16,437 --> 00:08:17,277
I'll have two.

134
00:08:17,277 --> 00:08:24,057
Uh, actually, just one's cool.

135
00:08:24,777 --> 00:08:26,277
Thank you, beautiful human!

136
00:08:29,777 --> 00:08:30,997
Bestie off ever!

137
00:08:31,997 --> 00:08:34,437
I'll be doing nothing but eating delicious sweets!

138
00:08:35,437 --> 00:08:35,917
Huh?

139
00:08:36,897 --> 00:08:37,377
Hello?

140
00:08:38,517 --> 00:08:39,757
What are you doing here?

141
00:08:39,757 --> 00:08:44,277
We wanted to go on a picnic, but we're not allowed to go far alone.

142
00:08:44,497 --> 00:08:45,357
We need an adult.

143
00:08:45,877 --> 00:08:46,877
Where's Miss Kobayashi?

144
00:08:47,217 --> 00:08:48,117
Oh, that's right.

145
00:08:48,177 --> 00:08:49,757
She did say they were making her work today.

146
00:08:51,237 --> 00:08:52,297
What about Toru?

147
00:08:53,177 --> 00:08:54,917
She said this letter's for you.

148
00:08:55,077 --> 00:08:55,537
Let's see.

149
00:08:57,557 --> 00:09:01,957
Kana watched a survival show, and now she wants to go to the mountains and pretend to search for food.

150
00:09:02,577 --> 00:09:05,737
I have to help out at the maid cafe today, so I can't go with her.

151
00:09:06,417 --> 00:09:08,717
I was hoping maybe you would take her instead.

152
00:09:09,757 --> 00:09:13,477
This means I do have some faith in you, so try to live up to it.

153
00:09:14,317 --> 00:09:16,177
Oh, you have faith in me?

154
00:09:16,837 --> 00:09:19,657
That condescending tone practically jumped off the page.

155
00:09:19,997 --> 00:09:20,977
Okay, let's go.

156
00:09:21,117 --> 00:09:22,137
The wilderness awaits!

157
00:09:22,677 --> 00:09:22,957
Yay!

158
00:09:23,637 --> 00:09:24,397
Good job!

159
00:09:24,457 --> 00:09:25,357
You did it, Kana!

160
00:09:33,697 --> 00:09:35,217
Let's set up our tent here.

161
00:09:37,097 --> 00:09:37,537
Sorry.

162
00:09:37,537 --> 00:09:42,297
We ran into Shota on our way to your house, and he asked to come to the mountains with us.

163
00:09:42,457 --> 00:09:43,377
I'm glad he did.

164
00:09:43,777 --> 00:09:45,137
So what are you two going to do now?

165
00:09:46,497 --> 00:09:46,937
Fish.

166
00:09:47,317 --> 00:09:48,597
We rented pools!

167
00:09:49,237 --> 00:09:49,617
Fishing?

168
00:09:50,277 --> 00:09:51,357
That takes me back.

169
00:09:52,177 --> 00:09:54,977
Long ago, I was the one fished.

170
00:09:54,977 --> 00:10:10,217
Okay, I'm bored.

171
00:10:10,297 --> 00:10:11,357
That was pretty fast.

172
00:10:11,597 --> 00:10:13,577
Is there a way we can speed these fish up?

173
00:10:13,737 --> 00:10:14,857
Using our hands?

174
00:10:15,137 --> 00:10:16,357
That might be more fun.

175
00:10:16,837 --> 00:10:18,077
Why don't you try further down?

176
00:10:18,797 --> 00:10:20,317
There are more fish in that area.

177
00:10:20,317 --> 00:10:26,477
Look, we caught one!

178
00:10:26,697 --> 00:10:28,717
Yeah, I think that's where I would have hidden, too.

179
00:10:29,477 --> 00:10:30,637
Hit for what?

180
00:10:36,557 --> 00:10:38,497
The curry and rice are ready, too.

181
00:10:39,377 --> 00:10:39,777
Yay!

182
00:10:39,777 --> 00:10:44,917
Chaperoning children isn't as hard as I thought.

183
00:10:47,737 --> 00:10:49,397
This curry's good.

184
00:10:49,697 --> 00:10:50,697
Thank you for the meal.

185
00:10:52,757 --> 00:10:54,277
That's a neat bug, Cyclone.

186
00:10:54,497 --> 00:10:55,177
Ew, gross!

187
00:10:55,217 --> 00:10:56,337
They seem to be having fun.

188
00:10:56,537 --> 00:10:57,617
I'm going to go relax a bit.

189
00:10:57,617 --> 00:11:05,777
Shotao, where are you going?

190
00:11:06,117 --> 00:11:06,557
Research.

191
00:11:06,977 --> 00:11:10,697
I've been doing a lot of reading lately about how to draw mana from the ley lines.

192
00:11:10,957 --> 00:11:13,477
They're supposed to be especially strong in the mountains.

193
00:11:13,837 --> 00:11:14,897
That sounds like fun.

194
00:11:15,477 --> 00:11:16,517
I want to go, too.

195
00:11:17,337 --> 00:11:18,577
Why the boys of the West?

196
00:11:18,577 --> 00:11:18,857
No!

197
00:11:22,697 --> 00:11:23,617
There's no way.

198
00:11:23,717 --> 00:11:24,757
They were just here.

199
00:11:24,937 --> 00:11:25,917
How did I lose them?

200
00:11:25,917 --> 00:11:28,257
They disappeared the moment I took my eyes off of them.

201
00:11:28,497 --> 00:11:29,977
I don't want to hear it!

202
00:11:30,337 --> 00:11:30,777
Wow.

203
00:11:30,937 --> 00:11:32,617
You couldn't handle taking them on a picnic?

204
00:11:32,977 --> 00:11:34,157
So lame.

205
00:11:35,757 --> 00:11:36,157
No!

206
00:11:36,757 --> 00:11:37,397
That's right.

207
00:11:37,517 --> 00:11:39,237
I completely forgot I have clairvoyance.

208
00:11:39,377 --> 00:11:40,437
I'll find them in no time.

209
00:11:44,017 --> 00:11:45,177
What's wrong, Shota?

210
00:11:45,877 --> 00:11:48,677
Someone just tried to hone in on us from a distant location.

211
00:11:49,177 --> 00:11:50,257
I'm sure it was Lukua.

212
00:11:50,477 --> 00:11:51,697
She does that sometimes.

213
00:11:52,037 --> 00:11:52,997
But I blocked it.

214
00:11:52,997 --> 00:11:56,017
Oh, you boys sure are silly.

215
00:11:56,297 --> 00:11:56,897
That's weird.

216
00:11:57,137 --> 00:11:58,317
Why can't I sense them?

217
00:11:59,537 --> 00:12:02,357
I never should have relied on you to do anything.

218
00:12:02,817 --> 00:12:03,677
Too bad.

219
00:12:05,897 --> 00:12:06,377
Lame.

220
00:12:08,377 --> 00:12:09,617
You guys!

221
00:12:11,517 --> 00:12:12,037
Come on.

222
00:12:12,117 --> 00:12:13,137
We should get back soon.

223
00:12:13,217 --> 00:12:15,797
If it gets dark, it's possible we could lose our way.

224
00:12:16,137 --> 00:12:17,157
Oh, we're fine.

225
00:12:17,357 --> 00:12:17,737
Chill.

226
00:12:17,897 --> 00:12:19,617
We followed the ley lines out here.

227
00:12:19,757 --> 00:12:21,417
We can just trace them again to get back.

228
00:12:22,057 --> 00:12:22,937
You boys.

229
00:12:31,477 --> 00:12:35,117
Actually, we left without saying anything to Miss Elma.

230
00:12:35,397 --> 00:12:36,577
We should get back soon.

231
00:12:37,517 --> 00:12:39,757
Did either of you hear that scream just now?

232
00:12:40,017 --> 00:12:41,477
Someone may have seen a bear.

233
00:12:41,477 --> 00:12:45,337
Okay, we made it.

234
00:12:47,017 --> 00:12:47,797
That's weird.

235
00:12:47,937 --> 00:12:48,717
She's not here.

236
00:12:49,257 --> 00:12:52,077
Did she get mad and go home because we left without telling her?

237
00:12:52,217 --> 00:12:54,537
She might have been worried and gone out to look for us.

238
00:12:56,737 --> 00:12:57,457
Damn it!

239
00:12:57,657 --> 00:12:58,617
Where could they be?

240
00:12:59,437 --> 00:13:00,437
You idiot!

241
00:13:00,897 --> 00:13:01,997
Well before me.

242
00:13:02,257 --> 00:13:03,177
So useless.

243
00:13:03,637 --> 00:13:06,677
I keep hearing Toru saying mean things to me in my head.

244
00:13:06,677 --> 00:13:09,117
Hi, excuse me.

245
00:13:09,257 --> 00:13:10,157
I'm looking for someone.

246
00:13:10,337 --> 00:13:11,677
Have you seen any children around here?

247
00:13:11,757 --> 00:13:12,577
There are three of them.

248
00:13:18,657 --> 00:13:19,557
How rude.

249
00:13:19,777 --> 00:13:21,017
Do you want to be eaten?

250
00:13:27,917 --> 00:13:29,757
If it's not one thing, it's another.

251
00:13:30,237 --> 00:13:31,277
Where could they be?

252
00:13:31,277 --> 00:13:31,817
Please!

253
00:13:36,677 --> 00:13:37,597
I'm looking!

254
00:13:41,417 --> 00:13:42,217
Connor, look!

255
00:13:42,337 --> 00:13:44,277
That's the one I saw in the river that time!

256
00:13:47,397 --> 00:13:49,497
Lady Elma, down here!

257
00:13:54,357 --> 00:13:55,437
We're sorry.

258
00:13:55,777 --> 00:13:56,917
You know you worried me.

259
00:13:57,577 --> 00:13:58,097
Yes.

260
00:13:58,477 --> 00:14:00,597
Lady Elma, for you.

261
00:14:01,637 --> 00:14:02,757
That's a pretty flower.

262
00:14:02,757 --> 00:14:04,337
I picked it for you.

263
00:14:04,437 --> 00:14:04,997
It's yours.

264
00:14:05,397 --> 00:14:06,997
I hope you can forgive us.

265
00:14:08,057 --> 00:14:08,397
Connor!

266
00:14:08,617 --> 00:14:09,677
I want a flower too!

267
